   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/limitless-adjudication-XXXXXX.ts\"",
    "output": "Confinement-failed baseline: promptLine=\"- test: `bun test` \u2014 already FAILING on the base branch (not your fault, fix only if in scope)\", candidate verdict=\"new_failure\", blocking=true. Ordinary failing baseline: identical promptLine, candidate verdict=\"still_failing\", blocking=false."
   },
   "evidence": "HEAD src/pipeline/prompts.ts:118\u2013120 finds the baseline check and uses only base && !base.ok to select the 'already FAILING ... fix only if in scope' message. The reproduction demonstrates that it conflates ordinary failures with unusable confinement results. Base contains exactly the same prompt logic and wording; base compareGates also blocked a failing candidate against this baseline, then with confinement_error. Thus the misleading guidance predates this change rather than becoming newly blocking. HEAD's subsequent gate feedback correctly explains why the baseline could not be compared, limiting the consequence to misleading initial guidance."
